From 86c6ed39a08cfcb55fb7f8a421c249ad12506d62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 20:55:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(legal): one operator record behind every surface that
 names the operator
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Why
---
shared/legal-entity.ts already gated the three legal pages, but the rest of
the product described the operator on its own:

  * the contact mailbox was typed out in the footer, the PDF report, the
    customer-confirmation fallback and ai.txt - four more places to forget
    when the address changes;
  * "Frankfurt am Main" was shown as the operator's location in the footer,
    the PDF ("Frankfurt · Deutschland"), the hero, and the structured data
    (Organization.address plus a LocalBusiness node with a PostalAddress,
    city-level areaServed and a priceRange) - while the record's city is
    empty. That is an invented operator fact, published to every crawler;
  * the imprint declared "nicht bereit und nicht verpflichtet" to consumer
    dispute resolution while the operator is unnamed. participates: false
    is the record's default, not anyone's declaration.

This patch makes the record the only source and adds read-only views:
contactEmail(), operatorName(), operatorLocality() and
disputeResolutionStatement(). Name, locality and the dispute declaration are
null until legalEntityPublishable(); the mailbox is shown before that because
LEGAL_ENTITY_PENDING_DE tells visitors to use it.

  * Footer: mailbox from the record; locality line only when publishable.
  * PDF footer: mailbox from the record; locality appended only when
    publishable (the brand line and site link are unchanged).
  * Hero label: the record's locality, else "Deutschland" (the market, not an
    operator address).
  * Impressum: dispute-resolution statement from the record, "wird ergänzt"
    until publishable; e-mail via contactEmail().
  * Confirmation email: reply-to falls back to LEGAL_ENTITY.email instead of
    a second literal.
  * ai.txt: Contact line from the record (omitted if there is none).
  * client/index.html: Organization.address and the LocalBusiness node
    removed. The contact email stays and is pinned to the record by test.
  * RUNBOOK: new "Operator identity" section documenting every field, what
    each surface shows while configured is false, and the release check.

Invariants preserved
--------------------
  * configured stays false; no name, street, city, phone, register entry or
    VAT id is invented. The mailbox value is unchanged.
  * Public legal pages say the details are being completed; they show no
    bracketed placeholder and no operator-only note (guards still pass).
  * Health reads the same record (0018): legal_entity stays a revenue blocker.
  * No statutory paragraph number added anywhere.
  * No change to routing, checkout, webhook, ledger or engines.

Tests added
-----------
  client/src/lib/legal-identity.test.ts (11 cases):
  * views: mailbox validity; name/locality withheld until publishable; the
    dispute default is not published; views agree with the shipped record.
  * tree guard over client/src, server, shared, scripts, api and
    client/index.html: the operator mailbox is spelled out only in the record
    and the static shell; any other address literal must be on a reasoned
    allowlist (default sender, input placeholders, a format example).
  * the static shell's addresses equal the record; no PostalAddress,
    LocalBusiness or addressLocality while the record is not publishable;
    no hard-coded operator city in shipped source.
  * every surface that names a contact imports shared/legal-entity.
  * RUNBOOK documents every field the release gate requires.
  client/src/lib/report-pdf.test.ts: the rendered PDF carries the record's
  mailbox and no invented city.

Not in this patch
-----------------
  * Filling the record or setting configured: true - operator facts.
  * Hard-coded vercel.app origin in index.html, report-pdf.ts and the build
    scripts (0020).
  * Rendering the operator's legal name in the PDF or confirmation email.
  * Removing HTML comments from the static shell (0021).

